{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The daughters of Tzelofḥad speak rightly.</b> The word כן means 'truly,' and its Aramaic translation is יאות ('fitting'). Happy is the one whose words the Holy One, blessed be He, affirms." "<b>You shall surely give them a possession of inheritance, etc.</b> Two portions: the portion of their father, who was among those who came out of Egypt, and his portion among the brothers in the estate of Ḥefer; for Tzelofḥad came out of Egypt at the age of twenty, and Ḥefer his father died in the wilderness. Therefore his daughters took the portion that belonged to their father among his brothers, since a daughter of a son stands in the place of a son to inherit with the brothers, as we have learned: וכל הקודם בנחלה יוצאי ירכו קודמין — 'and whoever precedes in inheritance, those who issued from his thigh precede.'" "<b>And you shall transfer the inheritance of their father to them.</b> Whatever Tzelofḥad was entitled to receive, his daughters shall receive. And Scripture used the language of העברה ('transfer') because a daughter transfers an inheritance from one tribe to another, for her son and her husband inherit her — since the commandment of לא תסב נחלה ('an inheritance shall not be turned aside') applied only to that generation alone. And likewise, והעברתם את נחלתו לבתו — 'and you shall transfer his inheritance to his daughter'; in all the other cases it says ונתת ('and you shall give'), but in the case of a daughter it says והעברת ('and you shall transfer')."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:26.961538010Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}